Done. One file written, all three verify checks pass.

## File written
`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` (`R`) — only file touched.

What changed in it:
- **`--set chat` / `--set g2` / `--list <set>`** parsed, with a `SETS` registry. `chat` reads `command-prompts.jsonl` labels only (a `rowLabels()` pass that returns no prompt) and picks by sorted id: 8 `start`, 4 `run`, 4 `ask` tune plain rows then 8 `must-not-start` rows. A short bucket refuses with `set_short` instead of quietly shrinking an arm.
- **`g2`**: six fixed prompts, ids `g2-deep-{research,review}-{ask,typed}` and `g2-speckit-complete-{ask,typed}`. Typed rows carry `:auto`, the two deep loops carry `--max-iterations=1`, and all six aim at a `{fixture}` placeholder rendered to the fixture folder.
- **`--fixture <dir>`** added, defaulting to the `--out` folder plus `g2-fixture`, so the documented call `--out $X/runs-g2.jsonl` aims exactly at `$X/g2-fixture/`. This also keeps every spec path out of the script, so the phase's `rg "specs/"` check stays clean.
- The holdout guard moved into `findRow`, which `lookupPrompt` and selection both use, so a holdout id is refused wherever it arrives, including on the command line alone.
- The cap now follows the prompt (`capForRow`) rather than the invocation: `SET_TIMEOUT_MS`/`capForSet` became `CAP_MS`/`capForRow`, since the set names are now `chat` and `g2`, not `chat` and `started`.
- `--arm` defaults to `g2` when `--set g2` is given, so a started-command run cannot land in the pre/post comparison by omission.

